[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-processing-decision :authorize-processing-run :proceed-with-processing-run :finalize-sterilization-clearance :declare-batch-sterilized-and-cleared :finalize-food-safety-clearance :declare-batch-fit-for-sale :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage" "2608100000-cloud-itonami-isic-1079-other-food-products-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the processing run" "proceed with the canning run" "authorize the processing run" "authorize the canning run" "finalize the processing decision" "declare the batch sterilized and cleared" "declare the batch sterilized" "finalize the sterilization clearance" "declare the batch fit for sale" "clear the batch for sale" "finalize the food safety clearance" "finalize the food-safety clearance" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007514, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/preservation-shop-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:preserver-verified :shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7514", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007514: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7514 Fruit, Vegetable and Related Preservers preservation-shop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7514\n-- Fruit, Vegetable and Related Preservers** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-7 already landed: ~42 occupations so far).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7514\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7514\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Fruit, Vegetable and Related Preservers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch (also cross-checked byte-exact\nagainst the raw `registry.edn` blob). Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7514` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nFruit, vegetable and related preservers can, pickle and preserve\nproduce -- real contamination risk if canning/sterilization protocols\nfail (botulism risk from improper canning). The controlling constraint\nfor this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include\nany op that directly finalizes a sterilization-clearance decision or a\nfood-safety-clearance decision (declaring a batch fit for sale), nor\noverride a shop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to\nPRESERVATION-SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never\nperforms preservation work or makes sterilization/food-safety-\nclearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\nclosely-related process-clearance safety pattern -- casting/pouring-\nexecution finalization and foundry-safety-officer-override exclusion,\nthe same structural shape this vertical needs for processing-\nexecution, sterilization-clearance and food-safety-clearance\nexclusion) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514` as an OSS\npreservation-shop scheduling/logistics-coordination actor for fruit,\nvegetable and related preservers, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Preservation Shop Coordination Advisor ⊣ PreserveCoordGovernor**\non a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a\ndifferent library coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the\nunrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **preservation-shop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct processing-execution or food-safety-\nclearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a processing-execution\ndecision, a sterilization-clearance decision, a food-safety-clearance\ndecision, or any override of a shop safety officer's judgment. These\nare not merely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent\nfrom the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/processing-schedule\n  scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a contamination-risk/\n  sterilization-failure/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates,\n  NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- produce/jarring-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nprocessing-execution decision, a sterilization-clearance decision, a\nfood-safety-clearance decision, or a shop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-processing-decision` or `:declare-batch-fit-for-sale`\ncannot even be proposed by the reference mock advisor (its\n`infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one of the four\nallowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a future LLM\nadvisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the governor's\nclosed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally\nand permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names nine concretely-forbidden ops\n(`preservecoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-processing-decision`, `:authorize-processing-run`,\n`:proceed-with-processing-run`, `:finalize-sterilization-clearance`,\n`:declare-batch-sterilized-and-cleared`,\n`:finalize-food-safety-clearance`, `:declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`preservecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-processing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-processing-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-processing-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-sterilization-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-sterilized-and-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nplus actor-level integration coverage\n(`preservecoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-sterilization-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-a-food-safety-clearance-op-even-at-high-confidence`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Preserver unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered preserver record (`:no-preserver`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the preserver is.\n2. **Shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered preservation-shop site (`:no-shop`). Together with check\n   1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/facility record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the nine\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a\n   processing/canning run, declaring a batch sterilized and cleared or\n   fit for sale, or overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a\n   second HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   processing-execution/sterilization-clearance/food-safety-clearance/\n   safety-override language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a contamination-risk/\n  sterilization-failure/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  shop safety or batch clearance.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  produce/jarring-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  processing-execution, sterilization-clearance, food-safety-clearance\n  or safety-officer-override attempt, which is why it is handled by a\n  different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"canning\", \"sterilization\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside\nthe mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a preservation-shop\ncoordination actor working adjacent to canning/sterilization work\nnecessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job)\ncould trigger if phrased carelessly. `preservecoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`\nis phrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g.\n\"proceed with the processing run\", \"declare the batch sterilized and\ncleared\", \"finalize the food-safety clearance\", \"override the shop\nsafety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`preservecoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for preserver ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nprocessing task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development.\n`preservecoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand its sterilization-clearance/food-safety-clearance siblings\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7514\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7514`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 29 tests, 63 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-batch-clearance` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  sterilization-clearance or food-safety-clearance decision exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe (botulism risk from improper canning/sterilization), the\n  capability itself must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a processing-execution, sterilization-\n  clearance or food-safety-clearance decision for later automatic\n  execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold produce/jarring-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the processing-execution/\n  sterilization-clearance/food-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"canning\"\n  \"sterilization\" \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known\n  self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked\n  example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to\n  phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  canning/sterilization/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Collapsing sterilization-clearance and food-safety-clearance into a\n  single excluded-decision category (mirroring 7211's single\n  casting/pouring-execution category): rejected -- the task's domain\n  design names three distinct excluded decision categories\n  (processing-execution, sterilization-clearance, food-safety-\n  clearance) plus a shop-safety-officer-judgment override, so this ADR\n  and the governor's `scope-excluded-ops`/`scope-excluded-phrases`\n  name all three explicitly rather than conflating them, giving each\n  its own dedicated unit test.\n- Merging `preserver` and `shop` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered preserver AND independently-registered\n  shop) matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/facility record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered preserver AND shop\n   (`:no-preserver`/`:no-shop`). Not a processing-execution,\n   sterilization-clearance or food-safety-clearance decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/processing-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a processing-execution,\n   sterilization-clearance or food-safety-clearance decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific processing run or batch clearance -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a contamination-risk/\n   sterilization-failure/equipment-condition concern to a\n   human/shop safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at\n   every confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the\n   ONLY channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced,\n   and it explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything\n   itself -- the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on\n   their own authority, including any sterilization-clearance or\n   food-safety-clearance decision.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- produce/jarring-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a processing-execution,\n   sterilization-clearance, food-safety-clearance or authorization\n   decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated\n   by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na processing-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\ncanning/processing run), a sterilization-clearance decision (e.g.\ndeclaring a batch sterilized and cleared), a food-safety-clearance\ndecision (e.g. declaring a batch fit for sale), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`preservecoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) nine\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`preservecoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`preservecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-processing-decision`\nand seven sibling tests), and (c) a content-based scope-exclusion\ncheck independent of the `:op` field\n(`preservecoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a processing run, declare a batch\nsterilized and cleared or fit for sale, or override a shop safety\nofficer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`preservecoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-processing-run`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-sterilization-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 29, :assertions 63, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Preservation Shop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :preserver-verification :shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7514", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7514], :test/simulator :preservecoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7514 — Fruit, Vegetable and Related Preservers Preservation-Shop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7514}]
